| name = Double Edge
| desc = [[Spell Block]] sources does not negate the self-damage component.
}}

 * {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
** Cannot self-{{M|deny}}.

* [[File:Dota2 Cast Range to AoE Visualization icon-6-1.png|84px]][[File:Dota2 Cast Range to AoE Visualization icon-6-2.png|84px]]
** Can affect enemy units at max {{Symbol|bonus cas}} {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} {{#expr:{{#var:Double Edge cast range}}+{{#var:Double Edge value1}}}}-distance away with the [[cast range]] and [[effect radius]].
** The ability effects are applied as follows within radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|P|21px]] :
**# {{cf|shdnotes}} 
**#* {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|centaur_doubleedge_slow}}
**# {{cf|shdnotes}}
**#* {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
**#** Grants a stack of percentage-based bonus based on Centaur's current total {{M|strength}} per affected hero within the damage radius.
**#** Considers {{M|clones}} as heroes, {{M|illusions}} and {{M|creep-heroes}} as creeps.
**# Applies the {{M|magical}} {{M|spell damage}} within the radius.
**# The self-damage.

{{Illusionnotes
| name = Retaliate
| desc = Non-functional.<br><br>{{Symbol|bonus t4r}} The created [[illusions]] now bestow the {{M|aura}}.
}}
{{Breaknotes
| name = Retaliate
| desc = Applies its ability effects on the attack before the [[Break]] source disables the ability.
}}

{{Illusionnotes
| name = Retaliate
| desc = Non-functional.<br><br>{{Symbol|bonus t4r}} The created [[illusions]] now bestow the {{M|aura}}.
}}
{{Breaknotes
| name = Retaliate
| desc = Applies its ability effects on the attack before the [[Break]] source disables the ability.
}}

 * The ability has the following properties:
** {{Symbol|Spell Damage}}
*** Retaliate's damage instance procs before the enemy successfully attacks Centaur, on both {{M|instant attacks}} and {{M|secondary attacks}}, regardless of distance.
*** Applies as a single damage instance in the {{M|combat log}} sourced to Centaur.
** {{Symbol|Strength}}
*** The [[strength]]-based bonus damage applied corresponds to the attacked unit's current strength.
** {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|centaur_return_aura}}
*** Retaliate is an {{M|aura}} that only affects Centaur by default.
*** {{cf|talnotes}} The {{ValueColor||aura|25tal}} {{M|talent|t=t4r}} considers allied {{M|clones}} and {{M|creep-heroes}} as heroes, {{M|illusions}} as creeps.

* {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} and {{Symbol|bonus t4r}} {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}}
** Affects the following allied units:
*** {{M|Invulnerable}} units.
** Does not affect the following allied units:
*** {{M|Hidden}} units.

* {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
** Affects the following unit's attacks:
*** {{M|Buildings}}
*** From {{M|allied units|x}}, Retaliate can {{M|deny}} the unit if the {{M|physical}} {{M|spell damage}} kills it.
** The following sources do not proc Retaliate:
*** [[Spell damage-based attacks]].
*** {{M|Instant attack}} sources that cannot proc {{M|attack modifiers}}:
**** {{A|Defiant Shell|Reciprocity}} 
**** {{A|Luna|Lunar Orbit}}
**** {{A|Medusa|Split Shot}} (without the {{M|Aghanim's Scepter|text=ability upgrade}}).
**** {{A|Gyrocopter|Flak Cannon}} 
**** {{A|Morphling|Waveform}}
*** {{U|Undying Zombie|text=Undying Zombies}} attacks.
*** {{M|Ward-type units}} attacks.

